86:
** Ἅιδης**
or ᾅδης, ου, ὁ, _Attic dialect_; _Epic dialect_ Ἀΐδης, α and ε; _Doric dialect_ Αΐδας, α, used by Trag., in Lyric poetryand _anapaest meter_: _genitive_ Αϊδος, _dative_ Αϊδι, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Homerus Epicus, Trag., see below: (perhaps ἀ- _privative_, ἰδεῖν):—in 8th c.BC: Homerus Epicus}} only as _proper name_ {{Refs 8th c.BC+|“Hades”, Ζεὺς καὶ ἐγώ, τρίτατος δ᾽ Αΐδης 8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 15.188, compare 8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Theogonia” 455:}} —εἰν᾽ Αΐδαο δόμοισι in the **nether** world, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Odyssea Homerus Epicus “Odyssey” 4.834}}; frequently εἰν, εἰς Αΐδαο (i.e. δόμοις, δόμους), as {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 22.389, 21.48; εἰν Ἄϊδος Il 24.593}}; Trag. and _Attic dialect_ ἐν Ἅιδου, εἰς Ἅιδου (i.e. οἴκῳ, οἶκον), {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Ajax” 865, 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Ranae” 69, etc.}}; Ἄϊδόσδε, _adverb_ **to the nether world**, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 7.330, etc.}}; παρ᾽ Ἅιδῃ, παρ᾽ Ἅιδην, {{Refs|“OT” 972, “OC” 1552:}} —hence,
**2** **place of departed spirits**, first in {{NT+8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 23.244 εἰσόκεν αὐτὸς.. Ἄϊδι κεύθωμα; ἐπὶ τὸν ᾅδην 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Cat.” 14; εἰς ἀΐδην “Anthologia Graeca” 11.23; ἐν τῷ ᾅδῃ NT.Luke.16.23.}}
**II** after {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Homerus Epicus}}, **the grave, death**, ἀΐδαν λαγχάνειν, δέξασθαι, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “P.” 5.96, “I.” 6(5).15}}; ᾅδης πόντιος **death** by sea, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 667, compare 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Alcestis” 13, “Hipp.” 1047}}; ᾅδου πύλη, Astrology texts, region below the Horoscope, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Vettius Valens Astrologus 179.13.}}
**II.2** _genitive_ ᾅδου with nouns in adjectival sense, **devilish**, θύουσαν ᾅ. μητέρ᾽{{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 1235; ᾅ. μάγειρος 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Cyclops” 397}}; **fatal, deadly**, δίκτυον, ξίφη ᾅ., {{Refs 8th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 1115, 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Orestes” 1399. [ᾰ 8th c.BC: Homerus Epicus}} in all forms except ᾱῐδος before vowels; ᾱῐδης {{Refs 7th c.BC+|7th-6th c.BC(?): Semonides Iambographus 7.117, probably in 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Oedipus Coloneus” 1689.]}}

87:
** ἀδιά-κρῐτος**, ον,
**undistinguishable, mixed**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “Κωακαὶ προγνώσιες” 570; αἷμα 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “de Somno et Vigilia” 458a21 (_comparative_)}}; **not discriminated**, {{Refs 5th c.AD+|5th-6th c.AD: Damascius Philosophus “de Principiis” 35.}}_adverb_ -τως **without distinction, in common**, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus “Fragmenta” 105 H., 5th c.AD: Hierocles Platonicus Philosophus “in Carmen Aureum - FPG” 12p.446M., 4th c.AD: Iamblichus Philosophus “de Mysteriis” 4.1, 6th c.AD: Justinianus Imperator “Novellae” 89.7.}}
**b** **promiscuous**, ἐπιμιξίαι{{Refs 1st c.BC+|1st c.BC: Dionysius Halicarnassensis 19.1.}}
**2** **unintelligible**, {{Refs 2nd c.BC+|2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 15.12.9.}}
**3** **undecided**, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “JTr.” 25, “OGI” 509.8 (from Aphrodisias).}}
**4** _active_, **not making due distinctions**, τὸ -τον{{Refs 1st c.AD+|1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 2.664.}}
**5** _adverb_ **-τως** **without examination,** {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|POxy. 715.36 (2nd c.AD).}}

90:
Related to: ** ἀδιά-φθορος**, ον,
**not affected by decay**, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Antyllus Medicus cited in 4th c.AD: Oribasius Medicus 46.22.3}}; **uncorrupted, chaste**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedrus” 252d; απ᾽ ὀρθῆς.. καὶ ἀδιαφθόρου τῆς ψυχῆς 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 18.298, compare 4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus 984, 1st c.BC: Diodorus Siculus Historicus 1.59, 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus 2.5e}}. _adverb_ -ρως, ἐρᾶσθαι{{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aeschines Orator 1.137.}}
**2** of judges, **incorruptible**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 768b}}; of witnesses, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Rhetorica” 1376a17}}; of magistrates, {{Refs|[prev. author] “Pol.” 1286a39 (_comparative_),compare “IG” 2.240b13. _superlative_}}_adverb_ -ώτατα Pl. [prev. cited]
**II** **imperishable**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedo” 106e.}}

91:
** ἀδῐκέω**,
_Aeolic dialect_ **ἀδικήω** {{Refs 7th c.BC+|7th-6th c.BC: Sappho Lyrica 1.20}}, _Doric dialect_ **ἀδικίω** {{Refs|“Tab.Heracl.” 1.138: _Ionic dialect_}}_imperfect_ ἠδίκεον or ἠδίκευν{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.121}}:—_passive_, _future_ in _middle_ form ἀδικήσομαι{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Iphigenia Aulidensis” 1436, 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 5.56, etc.; also ἀδικηθήσομαι 2nd c.AD: Apollodorus Damascenus Mechanicus 1.9.23, etc.}}: —**to be** ἄδικος, **do wrong** (defined by {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Rhetorica” 1368b6 τὸ βλάπτειν ἑκόντα παρὰ τὸν νόμον, compare ἀδίκημα), τῶν ἀδικησάντων τίσις ἔσσεται}}**those who have sinned,** {{Refs 5th c.BC+|Hymnus in Cererem 367; frequently in 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus}} and _Attic dialect_; τἀδικεῖν **wrong-doing**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Antigone” 1059}}; τὸ μὴ ἀδικεῖν **righteous dealing**, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Eumenides” 85, 749}}:— in legal phrase, **do wrong in the eye of the law**, the particular case being added in _participle_, as Σωκράτης ἀ... ποιῶν.. καὶ διδάσκων{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Apologia” 19b, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 1.1.1: with _accusative_ _cognate_, ἀδικίαν, ἀδικήματα, etc., 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Respublica” 344c, 409a, compare 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Rhetorica” 1389b7; also ἀ. οὐδὲν ἄξιον δεσμοῦ 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 3.145}}; ἀ. πολλά, μεγάλα, etc., {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Symposium” 188a, +others; οὐδέν, μηδὲν ἀ. [prev. work], +others:— ἀ. περὶ τὰ μυστήρια 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 21.175, compare “IG” 2.811c154}}; ἀ. εἰς πόλιν, κτῆμα, {{Refs 4th c.AD+|4th c.AD: Libanius Sophista “Orationes” 15.39, 31.7}}:—in games or contests, **play foul**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Nubes” 25, 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ethica Nicomachea” 1123b32.}}
**b** in _present_, **to be in the wrong**, εἰ μὴ ἀδικῶ γε if **I am** not **mistaken**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Charmides” 156a.}}
**II** _transitive_ with _accusative_ _person_, **wrong, injure**, {{Refs 7th c.BC+|7th c.BC: Archilochus Lyricus “Supp.” 2.13, 7th-6th c.BC: Sappho Lyrica 1.20, 5th c.BC: Epicharmus Comicus 286, 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.112, etc.}}:— **ruin**, of a girl, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus “Γεωργός” 30}}: with _double_ _accusative_, **wrong** one **in** a thing, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Plutus” 460; ἃ πολλοὺς ὑμῶν ἠδίκηκεν 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 21.129; μείζον᾽ ἢ ἐλάττονα ἀ. τινά 20.124; ἀ. ἀδικίαν περί τινας 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 854e}}:—_passive_, **to be wronged, injured**, μὴ δῆτ᾽ ἀδικηθῶ{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Oedipus Coloneus” 174; ἀ. εἴς τι 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Medea” 265; μέγιστα ἀ. 4th c.BC: Aeschines Orator 3.84; οὔτ᾽ ἀδικεῖ οὔτ᾽ ἀδικεῖται 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Symposium” 196b, etc.}}; _present_ ἀδικεῖται, -ούμενος used for the _perfect_ ἠδίκηται, -ημένος (see.{{Refs 5th c.BC+|above 1), 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 4.4.9, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Respublica” 359a}}: with _accusative_, **to be defrauded of**, μισθὸν ἀδικίας variant in {{NT|NT.2Pet.2.13.}}
**II.2** **harm, injure**, ἀ. γῆν{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 2.71, etc.; ἵππον 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “de Equitandi ratione” 6.3; especially in Medical sense, ἄνθρωπον 5th c.BC: Hippocrates Medicus “περὶ φύσιος ἀνθρώπου” 9; νεφρούς 3rd c.BC: Diphilus Siphnius Rerum Naturalium Scriptor cited in 2nd c.AD: Athenaeus Epigrammaticus 2.62f; τέμνειν καὶ θλᾶν καὶ ὁπωσοῦν ἄλλως ἀ. 2nd c.AD: Galenus Medicus “de Usu Partium” 13.8, compare 2nd c.AD: Archigenes Medicus cited in 3rd c.AD: Philumenus Medicus “de Venenatis Animalibus” 14.}}

92:
** ἀδίκ-ημα**, ατος, τό,
(ἀδικέω) **wrong done**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.2, 100, etc.}}: properly, **intentional wrong**, opposed to ἁμάρτημα and ἀτύχημα, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ethica Nicomachea” 1135b20f, “Rh.” 1374b8; ἀ. ὥρισται τῷ ἑκουσίῳ [prev. author] “EN” 1135a19}}: with _genitive_, **wrong done to**.., ἀ. τῶν νόμων{{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 21.225: also ἀ. πρός τινα 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Rhetorica” 1373b21; ἀ. εἴς τι 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 37.58; περί τι 1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus 2.159c:}} —ἐν ἀδικήματι θέσθαι to consider as **a wrong**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.35; ἀ. θεῖναί τι 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 14.37; ψηφίζεσθαί τι ἐν ἀ. εἶναι 4th c.BC: Hyperides Orator “pro Euxenippo” 20.}}
**2** **error of judgement**, uncertain in {{Refs 2nd c.BC+|2nd c.BC: Polybius Historicus 9.20a. 7.}}
**II** **that which is got by wrong, ill gotten goods**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Respublica” 365e, “Lg.” 906d.}}

93:
** ἀδικ-ία**,
_Ionic dialect_ -ιη, ἡ, **wrongdoing, injustice**, ἀδικίης ἄρχειν{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.130, compare 4.1, 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Orestes” 28, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Gorgias” 477c, +others; τύχἡ μᾶλλον ἢ ἀδικίᾳ 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 6.1}}; **'foul'** in racing, {{Refs|Anonymus “in SE” 30.15.}}
**II** **wrongful act, offence**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 6.136; καταγνόντες αὑτῶν ἀδικίαν 5th-6th c.BC: Andocides Orator 1.3:—in _plural_, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedo” 82a, etc.}}

94:
** ἄδῐκος**, ον,
(δίκη) of persons, **wrongdoing, unrighteous, unjust**: ἄνθρωποι{{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 260: _comparative_ -ώτερος [prev. work] 272; δίκαν ἐξ ἀδίκων ἀπαιτῶ 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Choephori” 398 (Lyric poetry)}}: _superlative_ **-ώτατος**{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Trachiniae” 1011 (Lyric poetry): ἄ. εἴς τι}} **unjust in** a thing, ἔς τινα **towards** a person, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.119; εἰς χρήματα 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 8.8.6; περί τινα [prev. work] 27}}; ἄ. [ἐν τῷ ἀστραγαλίζειν] one who **plays unfairly**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus Alcaeus1.110b}}: with _infinitive_, **so unjust as to.** NT.Heb.6.10.
**2** ἄ. ἵπποι **obstinate, unmanageable**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 2.2.26}}; ἄ. γνάθος the **hard** mouth of a horse, {{Refs|[prev. author] “Eq.” 3.5.}}
**II** of things, **unjust, unrighteous**, ἔργα{{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 334, 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.5; ἕργματα 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 380, 6th c.BC: Solon Lyricus 13.12; ἄδικα φρονέειν 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 395}}; ἄ. λόγος frequently in {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Nu.”}}; ἄρχειν χειρῶν ἀ. begin **an assault**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 4.2.1, 5th c.BC: Lysias Orator 4.11, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 1.5.13, 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 47.39}}; τὸ δίκαιον καὶ τὸ ἄ., τὰ δίκαια καὶ τὰ ἄ. right and **wrong**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Gorgias” 460a, etc.}}; πλοῦτος ἄ. **ill-gotten, unrighteous**, {{LXX+5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 1.38; ζυγὸν ἄ. LXX.Amos.8.5; νομὴ ἄ. οὐδὲν ἰσχύει “PTeb.” 286.7 (2nd c.AD)}}; ἡ ἄ... συναγωγὴ ἀνδρὸς καὶ γυναικός the **unrighteous** union, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Theaetetus” 150a}}; ἄ. δίκη **vexatious** suit, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Cratinus Comicus 19D.}}
**II.2** of the punishment of wrongdoing, Ζεὺς νέμων ἄδικα κακοῖς{{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Supplices” 404 (Lyric poetry), compare 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Orestes” 647.}}
**III** ἄ. ἡμέρα, i.e. ἄνευ δικῶν, a day **on which the courts were shut**, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Legal.” 9: δίκαιος ἄ.}} **who has not appeared in court**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Archippus Comicus 46.}}
**IV** _adverb_ **-κως**{{Refs 6th c.BC+|6th c.BC: Solon Lyricus 13.7, 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 1546; τοὺς ἀ. θνῄσκοντας 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Electra” 113 (_anapaest meter_)}}; εἴτε ὦν δὴ δικαίως εἴτε ἀ. **jure an injuria**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 6.137; δικαίως καὶ ἀ. 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 743b}}; οὐκ ἀ. not **without reason,** {{Refs 5th c.BC+|hymnus ad Mercurium 316, 4th-5th c.BC: Simonides Lyricus 89.3, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedo” 72a.}}

95:
Included with: ** ἄδῐκος**, ον,
(δίκη) of persons, **wrongdoing, unrighteous, unjust**: ἄνθρωποι{{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 260: _comparative_ -ώτερος [prev. work] 272; δίκαν ἐξ ἀδίκων ἀπαιτῶ 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Choephori” 398 (Lyric poetry)}}: _superlative_ **-ώτατος**{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Trachiniae” 1011 (Lyric poetry): ἄ. εἴς τι}} **unjust in** a thing, ἔς τινα **towards** a person, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.119; εἰς χρήματα 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 8.8.6; περί τινα [prev. work] 27}}; ἄ. [ἐν τῷ ἀστραγαλίζειν] one who **plays unfairly**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus Alcaeus1.110b}}: with _infinitive_, **so unjust as to.** NT.Heb.6.10.
**2** ἄ. ἵπποι **obstinate, unmanageable**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 2.2.26}}; ἄ. γνάθος the **hard** mouth of a horse, {{Refs|[prev. author] “Eq.” 3.5.}}
**II** of things, **unjust, unrighteous**, ἔργα{{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th-7th c.BC: Hesiodus Epicus “Opera et Dies” 334, 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.5; ἕργματα 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 380, 6th c.BC: Solon Lyricus 13.12; ἄδικα φρονέειν 6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 395}}; ἄ. λόγος frequently in {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Nu.”}}; ἄρχειν χειρῶν ἀ. begin **an assault**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 4.2.1, 5th c.BC: Lysias Orator 4.11, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Institutio Cyri (Cyropaedia)” 1.5.13, 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 47.39}}; τὸ δίκαιον καὶ τὸ ἄ., τὰ δίκαια καὶ τὰ ἄ. right and **wrong**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Gorgias” 460a, etc.}}; πλοῦτος ἄ. **ill-gotten, unrighteous**, {{LXX+5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 1.38; ζυγὸν ἄ. LXX.Amos.8.5; νομὴ ἄ. οὐδὲν ἰσχύει “PTeb.” 286.7 (2nd c.AD)}}; ἡ ἄ... συναγωγὴ ἀνδρὸς καὶ γυναικός the **unrighteous** union, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Theaetetus” 150a}}; ἄ. δίκη **vexatious** suit, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Cratinus Comicus 19D.}}
**II.2** of the punishment of wrongdoing, Ζεὺς νέμων ἄδικα κακοῖς{{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Supplices” 404 (Lyric poetry), compare 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Orestes” 647.}}
**III** ἄ. ἡμέρα, i.e. ἄνευ δικῶν, a day **on which the courts were shut**, {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Legal.” 9: δίκαιος ἄ.}} **who has not appeared in court**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Archippus Comicus 46.}}
**IV** _adverb_ **-κως**{{Refs 6th c.BC+|6th c.BC: Solon Lyricus 13.7, 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 1546; τοὺς ἀ. θνῄσκοντας 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Electra” 113 (_anapaest meter_)}}; εἴτε ὦν δὴ δικαίως εἴτε ἀ. **jure an injuria**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 6.137; δικαίως καὶ ἀ. 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 743b}}; οὐκ ἀ. not **without reason,** {{Refs 5th c.BC+|hymnus ad Mercurium 316, 4th-5th c.BC: Simonides Lyricus 89.3, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedo” 72a.}}

96:
** ἀδόκιμ-ος**, ον,
**not legal tender, not current**, of coin, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 742a}}; **not approved**, of horses, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Ἀθηναίων Πολιτεία” 49.1.}}
**2** **unsatisfactory, unconvincing**, of a statement, {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|3rd-2nd c.BC: Philo Mechanicus “(Belopoeica) Excerpte aus Philons Mechanik - Ath. Berl. Akad.” 76.47, 3rd c.AD: Alexander Aphrodisiensis Philosophus “in Aristotelis Topicorum libros octo commentaria - pars” 576.14.}}
**3** **disreputable**, λακίσματ᾽ ἀδόκιμ᾽ ὀλβίοις ἔχειν{{NT+5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Troades” 497; μοῦσα 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 829d, compare 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 25.36, NT.Rom.1.28}}. _adverb_ **-μως**{{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD(?): Pollianus Epigrammaticus 5.160.}}
**4** of persons, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Respublica” 618b}}; **discredited, reprobate**, {{NT+5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Respublica Lacedaemoniorum” 3.3 NT.2Tim.3.8, etc.}}

97:
** ἄδολος**, ον,
**guileless, honest**, σοφία{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “O.” 7.53}}; in _Attic dialect_especially of treaties, ἄ. εἰράνα{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Lysistrata” 169; σπονδαὶ ἄ. καὶ ἀβλαβεῖς 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 5.18.}}_adverb_, frequently in the phrase ἀδόλως καὶ δικαίως **without fraud** or covin, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 5.23, compare “IG” 1.42e; ἁπλόως καὶ ἀ. “GDI” 5024 (Gort.): generally, πλουτεῖν ἀδόλως “Scol.” 8}}; ἀδολώτερον λέγεσθαι, opposed to πιστότερον, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 3.3.4}}:— also, **genuinely, truly**, τεθνάκην ἀ. θέλω{{Refs 7th c.BC+|7th-6th c.BC: Sappho Lyrica “Papyrus fragments” in E. Diehl, 23.1, compare 3rd c.BC: Theocritus Poeta Bucolicus 29.32.}}
**II** **unadulterated, genuine**, χρίματος ἀδόλοισι παρηγορίαις{{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 95; στύραξ 1st c.AD: Dioscorides (Dioscurides) Medicus 1.66}}; χρυσός Eupolem. cited in {{Refs 1st c.BC+|1st c.BC: Alexander Polyhistor Historicus 18; ἀργύριον 2nd c.AD(?): Pollianus Epigrammaticus 3.86}}; σῖτος, πυρός, {{Refs|“PHib.” 1.85, “PGrenf.” 1.18; ἀ. ἀπὸ παντός [prev. work] 2.29.14: _metaphorically_, αὔραις ἀδόλοις}} **pure**, {{NT+5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Supplices” 1029 (Lyric poetry); τὸ λογικὸν ἄ. γάλα NT.1Pet.2.2.}}
**II.2** **unpretentious**, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|1st-2nd c.AD: Plutarchus Biographus et Philosophus “Pelopidas” 3.}}

99:
** Ἀδρίας**, ον,
_Ionic dialect_ Ἀδρίης, εω, ὁ, **the Adriatic**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 5.9, etc.}}:— _adjective_ Ἀδρι-ᾱνός, ή, όν, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Fragmenta - American Journal of Philology” 71}} also **Ἀδρι-ηνός**, κῦμα τᾶς Ἀδριηνᾶς ἀκτᾶς{{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 736 (Lyric poetry)}}: later, **Ἀδρι-ακός**, νέκταρ, of Italian wine, called {{Refs|“Adriatic”}} because imported through Corcyra, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|“Anthologia Graeca” 6.257 (1st c.AD: Antiphilus Epigrammaticus)}}: Ἀδριανικός, ἀλεκτορίδες{{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “de Generatione Animalium” 749b29: Ἀδριατικός, ὄρνιθες}} Chrysipp. Tyan. cited in {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Athenaeus Epigrammaticus 7.285d}}:—also _feminine_ **Ἀδρι-άς**, άδος
**A**, ἅλμη{{Refs 2nd c.AD+|2nd c.AD: Dionysius Periegeta 92.}}
